              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The labelled Pro Series serving is two scoops of about 82 g, which gives about 50 g of protein at the time of writing. That means one scoop is roughly 25 g of protein, a standard single dose. Calories run about 300 to 320 for the full serving depending on flavor, so a single scoop is roughly half that.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is Muscle Milk NSF Certified for Sport?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Per the brand, its protein powders are NSF Certified for Sport, and retailer listings for Pro Series and Genuine repeat the claim. The program screens for more than 270 banned substances and checks label accuracy. If you are a drug-tested athlete, confirm your exact product and flavor in the NSF Certified for Sport database before buying, because status can vary.
              </p>
